--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Read from the actual imports of this package. Pinned versions are in
pyproject.toml. Each keeps its own licence; none is redistributed here.

    torch, torchvision       tensors, networks, and the real attention path
    numpy                    the exchange format at every boundary
    trimesh                  assembles and writes the glTF that ships
    Pillow                   reads the photo, writes every produced image
    transformers             carries the image encoder and the cutout network
    huggingface_hub          fetches the cutout model when the cache is empty
    safetensors              reads the weight files
    opencv-python-headless   resizes, dilates, fills holes in the atlas
    scipy                    morphology on masks, gutters on the baked maps
    scikit-image             marching cubes for the structure preview
    einops                   tensor reshapes in the vendored code
    tqdm                     console progress during sampling and baking
    easydict                 the return type of the flow samplers
    nvidia-ml-py             reads what the card holds, past the allocator
    utils3d                  imported by the vendored TRELLIS.2 tree; installed
                             from git at a pinned revision, see pyproject.toml

The four view path adds one, and the single photo path runs without it:

    natten                   neighborhood attention, a compiled CUDA extension

Measuring the shot angles adds two more. Neither is in pyproject.toml: both sit
beside the weights, under models/multivue/cameras/, and multivue/cotes.py puts
that folder on sys.path at call time so nothing lands in your environment. See
docs/WEIGHTS.md.

    depth_anything_3         reads the angles from the four photographs
    omegaconf                reads that model's configuration

Three CUDA extensions, and the engine cannot run without them:

    o_voxel                  dual grid to mesh, and the PBR volume to UV bake
    cumesh                   remeshing, decimation, and the BVH used when baking
    flex_gemm                sparse convolution backend and 3D grid sampling

    They come from TRELLIS.2 and are installed by its setup.sh, but only
    one of the three lives in that repository. o_voxel is the o-voxel/
    subfolder of https://github.com/microsoft/TRELLIS.2, MIT, Copyright (c)
    Microsoft Corporation. cumesh is https://github.com/JeffreyXiang/CuMesh
    and flex_gemm is https://github.com/JeffreyXiang/FlexGEMM, both MIT,
    Copyright (c) 2025 Jianfeng Xiang. None of the three is on PyPI, and this
    repository does not ship them. Build them against torch 2.8.0+cu128 and
    Python 3.12. Be careful with one name: `pip install cumesh` succeeds and
    installs a different project of the same name, by Congjie He, which is not
    this one. Third-party Linux wheels exist at
    https://huggingface.co/siraxe/TRELLIS.2-4B_cuda_12.8.r12.8_wheels
    (cp312, linux_x86_64). They are not ours.

xformers
    This repository contains no xformers code and installs no xformers package.
    The vendored model asks for xformers as its sparse attention backend.
    sdpa_backend.py registers a stand-in module under that name and answers
    with PyTorch's own scaled dot product attention. Where a real xformers is
    already installed on the machine, the stand-in shadows the import and none
    of its kernels is called.

folder_paths and comfy.utils
    The vendored tree came from a ComfyUI node and still imports these two
    ComfyUI names. No ComfyUI code is included here. comfy_shim.py registers
    two small modules under those names, a models directory and a progress
    bar, both written for this project and Apache-2.0.

Libraries this engine does not use, on purpose
    nvdiffrast is under the NVIDIA Source Code License, research or evaluation
    only. It is called nowhere: uvraster.py rasterizes in PyTorch instead, on
    every path that used to reach for it, in the vendored code as much as in
    ours. The o_voxel wheel still imports nvdiffrast at module level, so
    leurre_nvdiffrast.py registers the two module names it asks for; the
    objects inside them raise if anything ever calls them, and contain no
    NVIDIA code.

    pymeshlab (GPL-3.0) and meshlib (a non-commercial and education agreement,
    AMV Consulting) are neither imported nor called. The meshlib decimation of
    the vendored mesh class was deleted from this repository on 10 September
    2026, not merely left unused.

Two GPL-3.0 names left in the vendored tree
    _vendu_trellis2/trellis2/pipelines/trellis2_image_to_3d.py names mmgp
    (deepbeepmeep/mmgp) inside a try/except, and
    _vendu_trellis2/trellis2/utils/mesh_utils.py imports plyfile
    (dranjan/python-plyfile) at module level. Neither package is installed or
    redistributed by this repository, and nothing in the package imports
    mesh_utils. If you install either one, its own licence applies to what you
    then distribute.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the engine downloads by itself
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

One piece: BiRefNet_HR, the cutout model. matting.py loads it from transformers
by its Hugging Face id, with trust_remote_code=True, at the first generation if
the cache is empty. Remote code is executed at that moment. Every other weight
set has to be placed by hand under <LOCALMESH_ROOT>/models/. The tree, file by
file, is in docs/WEIGHTS.md.

The vendored TRELLIS.2 tree can fetch two more, on the Pixal3D recipe alone,
which the command line does not offer: MoGe-2 through snapshot_download
(https://huggingface.co/Ruicheng/moge-2-vitl, MIT) and NAF through
torch.hub.load("valeoai/NAF") (Apache License 2.0).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No weights are stored in this git repository. The engine reads them from its
runtime root, named by the LOCALMESH_ROOT environment variable, under
<root>/models/; LUMENGEN_ROOT is read after it, for installations that predate
the name. The sets we convert ourselves are published apart from the code, on
Hugging Face:

    https://huggingface.co/Qtn-Cls/LocalMeshEngine

Each set keeps the licence of its author.

TRELLIS.2-4B, FP8 conversion
    https://huggingface.co/visualbruno/TRELLIS.2-4B-FP8
    MIT License. Original model: Microsoft Research, MIT License.

TRELLIS-image-large, sparse structure decoder
    https://huggingface.co/microsoft/TRELLIS-image-large
    MIT License, Microsoft.

BiRefNet_HR, subject cutout
    https://huggingface.co/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet_HR
    MIT License.

    The stock TRELLIS.2 descriptor cuts the background with briaai/RMBG-2.0,
    which is gated and non-commercial. This engine writes that one field into a
    side-car configuration and uses BiRefNet_HR instead, which is the same
    architecture under MIT. RMBG is never loaded.

Pixal3D multi-view, the four view structure and shape cascade
    https://github.com/TencentARC/Pixal3D
    https://huggingface.co/TencentARC/Pixal3D
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Tencent.

    WE CONVERT THESE OURSELVES. The three files the four view path loads
    are our FP8 conversions of the official BF16 weights:

        structure_mv_fp8.safetensors
        forme_512_mv_fp8.safetensors
        forme_1024_mv_fp8.safetensors

    They are not in this git repository. They are served from
    https://huggingface.co/Qtn-Cls/LocalMeshEngine. Tencent's MIT text and
    their notice travel with the code, in this repository, as
    _vendu_trellis2/LICENSE-Pixal3D and _vendu_trellis2/NOTICE-Pixal3D. The
    conversion is lossy and measured: weight RMSE 0.025 to 0.026 against the
    source, projection probe 0.027.

NAF (Neighborhood Attention Field), the field network of the four view path
    https://github.com/valeoai/NAF
    Apache License 2.0. Valeo.ai, Sorbonne Universite, CNRS.

    champ.safetensors is the official checkpoint, used unmodified. It is served
    from https://huggingface.co/Qtn-Cls/LocalMeshEngine. The Apache License 2.0
    that covers it is in this repository, at multivue/champ/LICENSE.

Depth Anything 3 (DA3-BASE), the shot angles
    https://huggingface.co/depth-anything/DA3-BASE
    Apache License 2.0, code and weights.

    It reads two things from the four photographs: the azimuth each one was
    taken from, and which side each profile shows. The measured azimuths then
    drive the projection. When it is absent the engine falls back to the
    nominal angles, 0, 90, 180 and 270 degrees, and says so in the result.

    Its source tree and the three small pure-Python packages it needs
    (omegaconf, addict, antlr4-python3-runtime) sit beside its weights, under
    cameras/source/src and cameras/deps, rather than in the environment, so
    installing this module cannot disturb an existing installation. They are
    not redistributed here and keep their own licences.

DINOv3 ViT-L/16, image encoder
    https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vitl16-pretrain-lvd1689m
    DINOv3 License, Meta Platforms, Inc.
    https://ai.meta.com/resources/models-and-libraries/dinov3-license/

    THIS ONE HAS CONDITIONS, AND THEY ARE NOT OPTIONAL. Anyone redistributing
    these weights must ship a copy of the agreement with them, require the
    recipient to accept the same terms, and display "Built with DINOv3"
